          "text": "The dominant reflections index as a tetragonal, cation-ordered rocksalt derivative. A \\(\\sqrt5\\times\\sqrt5\\) ordering of the alkali sublattice gives space group **I4/m** (No. 87), \\(Z=2\\), with approximately:\n\n\\[\na=9.8585\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\qquad c=6.2954\\ \\text{\u00c5}.\n\\]\n\nThe close intense pair near \\(28.3^\\circ\\) corresponds principally to 002 and the 310 family; their higher harmonics account for the strong groups near 40.7, 58.6\u201359.2, and 66\u201367\u00b0. The very weak additional features may indicate minor strain, slight symmetry lowering, or a small secondary component, but they do not warrant a separate chemically distinct model.\n\n```cif\ndata_K4NaCl5\n_audit_creation_method              'Indexed and derived from powder XRD'\n_chemical_name_common               'potassium sodium chloride, ordered'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'K4NaCl5'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'K8 Na2 Cl10'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               2\n\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M       'I 4/m'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number          87\n\n_cell_length_a                       9.8585\n_cell_length_b                       9.8585\n_cell_length_c                       6.2954\n_cell_angle_alpha                    90\n_cell_angle_beta                     90\n_cell_angle_gamma                    90\n_cell_volume                         611.9\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type               'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength         1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1   'x,y,z'\n2   '-y,x,z'\n3   '-x,-y,z'\n4   'y,-x,z'\n5   'x,y,-z'\n6   '-y,x,-z'\n7   '-x,-y,-z'\n8   'y,-x,-z'\n9   'x+1/2,y+1/2,z+1/2'\n10  '-y+1/2,x+1/2,z+1/2'\n11  '-x+1/2,-y+1/2,z+1/2'\n12  'y+1/2,-x+1/2,z+1/2'\n13  'x+1/2,y+1/2,-z+1/2'\n14  '-y+1/2,x+1/2,-z+1/2'\n15  '-x+1/2,-y+1/2,-z+1/2'\n16  'y+1/2,-x+1/2,-z+1/2'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n